/-!
# Exact binary septic coefficient data

The three integer coordinates are the coefficients of `1`, `p`, and `p²`,
with common denominator `50803200000`. The word order is multiplication order.
The nested rows use outermost-to-innermost right-nested commutators.
Letter `0` represents `a` and letter `1` represents `b`. The source nested
triples are the binary `M7`, `N7`, and `L7` entries of
`artifacts/trotter/paper/supplement/suzuki4_septic_certificate_20261027.json`.
Back-expansion of these static tables and identification with actual product
coefficients are separate theorems.

## Main definitions

* `nestedDefectData`, `nestedCenteredData`, `nestedBchData`: the 32 right-nested rows.
* `expandedDefectData`, `expandedCenteredData`, `expandedBchData`: all 128 word positions.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace FQFP.SuzukiSepticCertificate

/-- Three integer parameter coefficients with the common septic denominator. -/
abbrev Triple := ℤ × ℤ × ℤ

/-- A binary word with its constant, linear, and quadratic parameter coefficients. -/
abbrev Rows := List (List (Fin 2) × Triple)

/-- The common denominator of all three binary septic presentations. -/
def denominator : ℕ := 50803200000

/-- The seven-bit binary word, most significant bit first. -/
def binaryWord (n : ℕ) : List (Fin 2) :=
  (List.range 7).reverse.map fun k ↦ Fin.ofNat 2 (n / 2 ^ k)

